  "Question": "Given \\(a<b\\), which of the following inequalities must hold?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(a-2<b-2\\)",
    "B": "\\(-a<-b\\)",
    "C": "\\(3a>3b\\)",
    "D": "\\(a/(-2)<b/(-2)\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Subtracting 2 from both sides leaves the direction unchanged. Multiplying or dividing by a negative number reverses the direction, so B and D should be \\(-a>-b\\) and \\(a/(-2)>b/(-2)\\), respectively. Multiplying by the positive number 3 leaves the direction unchanged, so C is incorrect.",
